{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1788112103,"nonce":"W1HBBQ4EkpIEfXxP3zxayKLL12I=","title":"5.1 rwtest runner + assertion helpers","message":"Wave 5 — payoff. Depends: 1.2, 1.3, 1.4 (2.x/3.x widen what's assertable but\ndon't gate the runner). Python, in rimworld-tools.\n\n## Goal\n`rwtest`: scenario scripts in, pass/fail + evidence out. The mod-testing\nproduct the whole platform exists for.\n\n## Context (read first)\n- DESIGN.md §rwtest §Journal; 1.4 (rwa is the only game interface); log-\n  watcher/queue (what quarantine means — do NOT feed it by default)\n- pytest's shape (fixtures/asserts/reports) as the ergonomic north star —\n  but standalone runner first, pytest plugin only if trivial\n\n## Scope\n- Scenario format (python preferred over yaml for composability): declares\n  bench_version required, fixture (save name | gen-script of rwa/dev calls),\n  acts (rwa calls), advance specs, assertions.\n- Assertion helpers: event_within(type/filter, tick-window),\n  eventually_state(query, predicate, window), never_event(filter),\n  state_equals/approx, no_red_errors (implicit default — opting OUT is loud).\n- Game lifecycle: ensure bench running (boot via run-agent.sh if not), fresh\n  load of the fixture per scenario, kill/reuse policy, timeout watchdog.\n- Fixtures: saves stored under the bench config with bench-version tags\n  (DESIGN §Bench); mismatch = hard error offering regen; gen-scripts\n  re-create them.\n- Report: per-scenario pass/fail + evidence (journal excerpts, digests,\n  failing assertion context), md summary + machine-readable (exit codes for\n  orchestrator/CI). Run artifacts into RUNS/, never the triage queue.\n\n## Invariants\nProperty-based within windows, never byte-exact; every scenario carries\nno_red_errors unless explicitly waived with a reason string; runner never\ntouches game internals except through rwa.\n\n## Open questions (worker's)\nScenario API surface (keep v1 small); parallel scenarios (probably no — one\ngame); flaky-test policy (rerun-once? quarantine label?).\n\n## Acceptance\n- Self-test suite: a passing scenario, a failing-assertion scenario, a\n  red-error-detection scenario, a bench-version-mismatch scenario — all\n  reported correctly with correct exit codes.\n- A worked example test against vanilla behavior (e.g. \"growing zone feeds\n  colony\": fixture farm → advance 3 days → harvest events + food-days rises)\n  runs green on the bench.","files":null}]}